# The RFC-049 audits hash these trees byte for byte (frozen specifications, vendor
# snapshots, retrieved primary-source evidence).  Git's automatic end-of-line
# normalisation would rewrite those bytes on checkout and silently break every
# recorded digest, so the trees are stored exactly as they are on disk.
data/rfc049/** -text

# The cost-barrier CI evidence bundle is digest-pinned: the copy of the gitignored
# market-horizon input must arrive in a clean checkout with exactly the bytes the
# published explorer recorded for it, so git must not normalise them on the way in
# or out.  Same reason as the RFC-049 trees above, same treatment.
data/recovery/wp7/evidence/** -text

# The WP-8 input-authority bundle is digest-pinned for the same reason as the
# cost-barrier one: every external input the ACTIVE recovery lane needs must arrive
# in a clean checkout with exactly the bytes its published artefact recorded, so git
# must not normalise them on the way in or out.
data/recovery/wp8/evidence/** -text

# The admission chain is digest-pinned by the ledger that quotes it: `config/strategy_admission.json`
# records the SHA-256 of the discovery results and of the admission matrix, and the WP-7 cost-barrier
# explorer pins the ledger itself.  Those digests are hashes of the committed bytes, so a checkout
# that normalises line endings changes the file and breaks the anchor without touching its content.
# That is what happened on a Windows host whose system-wide `core.autocrlf=true` turned all 614
# lines of the matrix into CRLF: the ledger's test then failed with a digest mismatch on a checkout
# nobody had edited.  Pinning the four files keeps the chain verifiable wherever it is cloned.
config/strategy_admission.json -text
docs/STRATEGY_ADMISSION_MATRIX.json -text
docs/STRATEGY_DISCOVERY_V3_RESULTS.json -text
docs/COST_MODEL_V3.json -text

# The WP-006 economic data and its evidence are digest-pinned the same way.  The
# manifest records the SHA-256 of every dataset, and the engine refuses to evaluate a
# dataset whose bytes differ from it; the independent verification records the digest
# of the results and trade file it reviewed.  A checkout with `core.autocrlf=true`
# rewrites those bytes and turns every one of those anchors into a false alarm on a
# clean clone, so both trees are stored exactly as they are on disk.
data/economic/** -text
docs/agentic/economic_audit/WP-ECONOMIC-RECOVERY-006/evidence/results/** -text
